# Issue 1 — Wrong Place for Common Data ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

Currently,

```java
CurrentAccount
       |
AccountDTO
```

and

```java
SavingsAccount
       |
AccountDTO
```

Every account owns an `AccountDTO`.

That means

```java
CurrentAccount
{
   AccountDTO acc1;
}
```

Instead, the `Account` class itself should contain the common fields.

Like this:

```java
abstract class Account {

    protected String accountNo;
    protected String customerName;
    protected double balance;

}
```

Then

```java
class SavingsAccount extends Account
```

already has

```
accountNo

customerName

balance
```

No DTO required.

This is much cleaner OO design.

---

# Issue 2 — Missed `super` Usage ⭐⭐⭐⭐

The requirements mentioned using `super`.

You only have

```java
super.displayBalance();
```

inside the FD constructor.

That line shouldn't be there.

It prints

```
No Valid Account to show Balance
```

during object creation.

That isn't meaningful.

Instead,

```java
abstract class Account {

    Account(String accNo,String name,double bal){

    }
}
```

Then

```java
SavingsAccount(...)
{
    super(accNo,name,bal);
}
```

This is what interviewers expect.

